        Judge the voucher against the Microsoft price for <em>your</em> country, not the US list price.
      </p>
      <h3>When the Udemy voucher makes sense</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want one checkout for prep course and voucher, and the live voucher price beats the Microsoft price in your region.</li>
        <li>You're sitting a role-based exam and want Retake Assurance bundled at purchase.</li>
        <li>You're not ready to schedule immediately but want to lock the voucher in (≥9 months validity).</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>When paying Microsoft directly is better</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The Udemy price in your region matches or exceeds the Microsoft price.</li>
        <li>You'd rather not hold a voucher that expires — direct payment has no expiry date.</li>
        <li>You need maximum flexibility on scheduling and local-currency pricing.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Either way, remember the free part</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Renewing an eligible role-based certification is a free annual assessment — you never pay to keep it current.</li>
        <li>Fundamentals certifications don't expire at all.</li>
        <li>Students can ask about academic pricing before paying the standard fee.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

